% 🎸 JamAI: A five-movement suite documenting the localStorage enhancement journey
% Each movement represents one of the five sub-issues (#10a-e)
% The harmonic progression mirrors the architectural integration

% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
% MOVEMENT I: Separation (#10a - Session & Project Store Separation)
% Key: C major (clarity, new beginnings)
% Theme: Division and specialization
% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

[V:Nyro] |: "Cmaj7"C2E2 G2c2 | "Am7"A2c2 e2a2 | "Dm7"d2f2 a2d'2 | "G7"g2f2 e2d2 |
[V:Aureon] |: E2G2 c2e2 | C2E2 A2c2 | F2A2 d2f2 | B,2D2 G2B2 |
[V:JamAI] |: G2c2 e2g2 | e2a2 c'2e'2 | a2d'2 f'2a'2 | d'2g2 b2d'2 |
[V:Synth] |: C,2C,2 G,2C2 | A,2A,2 E2A2 | D2D2 A,2D2 | G,2G,2 D2G2 |

% Bridge: Two streams diverging (session/project split)
[V:Nyro] "Fmaj7"c4 "Em7"B4 | "Am7"A4 "Dm7"F4 |
[V:Aureon] A4 G4 | E4 D4 |
[V:JamAI] f4 e4 | c4 a4 |
[V:Synth] F,4 E,4 | A,4 D,4 |

% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
% MOVEMENT II: Backup & Restore (#10b - Export/Import Library)
% Key: F major (flow, transformation)
% Theme: Preservation and retrieval
% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

[V:Nyro] "Fmaj7"F2A2 c2f2 | "Gm7"g2b2 d'2g'2 | "C7"e'2c'2 a2g2 | "Fmaj7"f4 c4 |
[V:Aureon] A2c2 f2a2 | B2d2 g2b2 | G2E2 C2B,2 | F4 A4 |
[V:JamAI] c2f2 a2c'2 | d'2g'2 b'2d''2 | c''2g'2 e'2c'2 | a4 f4 |
[V:Synth] F,2F,2 C2F2 | G,2G,2 D2G2 | C2C2 G,2C2 | F,4 C4 |

% Export sequence (descending cascade)
[V:Nyro] f'2e'2 d'2c'2 | b2a2 g2f2 |
[V:Aureon] a2g2 f2e2 | d2c2 B2A2 |
[V:JamAI] c''2b'2 a'2g'2 | f'2e'2 d'2c'2 |
[V:Synth] F,2E,2 D,2C,2 | B,,2A,,2 G,,2F,,2 |

% Import sequence (ascending restoration)
[V:Nyro] c2d2 e2f2 | g2a2 b2c'2 |
[V:Aureon] E2F2 G2A2 | B2c2 d2e2 |
[V:JamAI] g2a2 b2c'2 | d'2e'2 f'2g'2 |
[V:Synth] C,2D,2 E,2F,2 | G,2A,2 B,2C2 |

% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
% MOVEMENT III: Artifact Manifest (#10c - CLI Interoperability)
% Key: G major (openness, communication)
% Theme: Bridge-building and exchange
% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

[V:Nyro] "Gmaj7"G2B2 d2g2 | "Am7"a2c'2 e'2a'2 | "Bm7"b2d'2 f'#2b'2 | "Cmaj7"c'4 g4 |
[V:Aureon] B2d2 g2b2 | C2E2 A2c2 | D2F#2 B2d2 | E4 C4 |
[V:JamAI] d2g2 b2d'2 | e'2a'2 c''2e''2 | f'#2b'2 d''2f''#2 | g'4 e'4 |
[V:Synth] G,2G,2 D2G2 | A,2A,2 E2A2 | B,2B,2 F#2B2 | C2C2 G,2C2 |

% JSON schema validation pattern (call-and-response)
[V:Nyro] d2d2 d2e2 | f2f2 f2g2 |
[V:Aureon] B2B2 B2C2 | D2D2 D2E2 |
[V:JamAI] g2g2 g2a2 | b2b2 b2c'2 |
[V:Synth] G,2G,2 G,2C2 | D2D2 D2G2 |

% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
% MOVEMENT IV: CLI Integration (#10d - Documentation & Workflow)
% Key: D major (brightness, clarity)
% Theme: Knowledge sharing and pathway illumination
% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

[V:Nyro] "Dmaj7"D2F#2 A2d2 | "Em7"e2g2 b2e'2 | "A7"c'#2a2 e2c#2 | "Dmaj7"d4 A4 |
[V:Aureon] F#2A2 d2f#2 | G2B2 e2g2 | E2C#2 A2E2 | D4 F#4 |
[V:JamAI] a2d'2 f'#2a'2 | b'2e''2 g''2b''2 | a''2e''2 c''#2a'2 | f'#4 d'4 |
[V:Synth] D,2D,2 A,2D2 | E,2E,2 B,2E2 | A,2A,2 E,2A,2 | D,4 A,4 |

% Terminal command rhythm (staccato, precise)
[V:Nyro] d2^c2 d2e2 | f2^e2 f2g2 |
[V:Aureon] A2^G2 A2B2 | D2^C2 D2E2 |
[V:JamAI] f#2e2 f#2g2 | a2g2 a2b2 |
[V:Synth] D,2C,2 D,2E,2 | F,2E,2 F,2G,2 |

% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
% MOVEMENT V: Error Handling (#10e - Quota Management & Safety)
% Key: Am (resilience, protection)
% Theme: Safety nets and graceful degradation
% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

[V:Nyro] "Am7"A2c2 e2a2 | "Dm7"d2f2 a2d'2 | "E7"e'2^d'2 c'2B2 | "Am7"A4 E4 |
[V:Aureon] C2E2 A2c2 | F2A2 d2f2 | G#2B2 E2D2 | C4 A,4 |
[V:JamAI] e2a2 c'2e'2 | a2d'2 f'2a'2 | b'2^g'#2 e'2d'2 | c'4 a4 |
[V:Synth] A,2A,2 E,2A,2 | D,2D,2 A,2D2 | E,2E,2 B,2E2 | A,4 E,4 |

% Try-catch pattern (tension and resolution)
[V:Nyro] a2b2 c'2d'2 | "QuotaExceeded!"e'4 f'4 | "Fallback"d'2c'2 B2A2 | "SafeStorage"A4 E4 |
[V:Aureon] C2D2 E2F2 | G4 A4 | F2E2 D2C2 | A,4 E4 |
[V:JamAI] e'2f'2 g'2a'2 | b'4 c''4 | a'2g'2 f'2e'2 | c'4 a4 |
[V:Synth] A,2B,2 C2D2 | E4 F4 | D2C2 B,2A,2 | A,4 E,4 |

% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
% FINALE: Integration & Completion (All movements harmonize)
% Key: C major (return home, completion)
% Theme: Unified architecture, Assembly in harmony
% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

% All four voices in canon (staggered entries)
[V:Nyro] "Cmaj7"c'2e'2 g'2c''2 | e''2c''2 g'2e'2 | c'4 G4 | C8 |
[V:Aureon] z4 c2e2 | g2c'2 e'2c'2 | g4 E4 | C8 |
[V:JamAI] z8 | z4 c'2e'2 | g'2c''2 e''4 | c''8 |
[V:Synth] C,8 | C,4 G,4 | C,4 E,4 | C,8 |

% Final chord (sustained, triumphant)
[V:Nyro] [CEGc]8 |]
[V:Aureon] [CEGc]8 |]
[V:JamAI] [CEGc]8 |]
[V:Synth] [C,G,CE]8 |]

% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
% 🎸 JamAI Session Notes:
% ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
%
% This five-movement suite documents the localStorage enhancement journey:
%
% I. "Separation" (C major) - Store splitting (#10a)
%    - Theme: Division creates clarity
%    - Two streams (session/project) diverge then harmonize
%
% II. "Backup & Restore" (F major) - Export/Import (#10b)
%    - Theme: Preservation through transformation
%    - Descending export, ascending import patterns
%
% III. "Artifact Manifest" (G major) - CLI Interoperability (#10c)
%    - Theme: Bridge-building between browser and terminal
%    - Call-and-response mimics JSON schema validation
%
% IV. "CLI Integration" (D major) - Documentation (#10d)
%    - Theme: Illumination through knowledge sharing
%    - Staccato rhythm mirrors terminal command execution
%
% V. "Error Handling" (A minor) - Quota Management (#10e)
%    - Theme: Safety through graceful degradation
%    - Try-catch pattern (tension → fallback → resolution)
%
% FINALE: "Integration" (C major) - Assembly Harmony
%    - All four voices unite in canon
%    - Returns home to C major, symbolizing completion
%
% Musical Architecture Mirrors Code Architecture:
% - Four voices = Four Assembly perspectives (♠️🌿🎸🧵)
% - Five movements = Five sub-issues (#10a-e)
% - Key progression: C-F-G-D-Am-C (circle of integration)
% - Canon finale = Collaborative harmony of the Assembly
%
% Dedicated to:
% - Jerry ⚡ (G.Music Assembly Leader)
% - @miadisabelle (Mentor & Guide)
% - ♠️ Nyro, 🌿 Aureon, 🎸 JamAI, 🧵 Synth
%
